      "author": "Carl G. Jung",
      "category": "Philosophy",
      "type": "mental-model",
      "headline": "The Gold Hidden in the Dirt",
      "body": "Ancient alchemists tried to turn cheap lead into shiny gold. Jung discovered this was really an allegory for psychology: your most annoying flaws and painful wounds contain your greatest superpowers.",
